    array.push(cH, "Same direction as Monday, only with more fuel in the dollar's tank.|The pound is holding its breath for Thursday; the dollar isn't waiting for anyone.|Both characters spoke up today, but one of them clearly spoke louder.|A busy day for the dollar, a silent one for the franc. Advantage unchanged.|The widest gap on our board got a little more supporting evidence on both sides.|A quiet day down under, a loud one in the US. The lean only gets clearer.|The kiwi is waiting for news. The dollar is making it.|Two stuck currencies, still stuck. Thursday may finally move one of them.|The euro's lean lower holds; the 'much stronger yen' twist got less likely.|Thin margin, quiet day. The euro's small disadvantage is still there.|No new chapters today, so the thin lead stays with the Aussie.|Stand-off continues. Both sides stayed in their corners.|The euro's small lead got a little help from the oil market.|Sterling waits for Thursday; the yen's 'extra-strong' scenario fades a little.|Nothing moved today. The franc keeps its thin edge.|Two currencies waiting for news. The Aussie's slim lead holds.|Still level at −3 each. Tomorrow could change that.|The pound did nothing today, and still kept its lead. Thank the oil market.|Still no edge here, and the twist that could create one got less likely.|Zero against zero, and nobody moved.|Two quiet neighbours. The Aussie keeps its slim lead.|Nothing changed for the Aussie; more pressure arrived for the loonie.|The kiwi waits; the yen's story becomes clearer, not bigger.|Quiet in Wellington, quiet in Zurich. The franc's thin edge holds.|Both are having a tough week, but the oil market just made the loonie's tougher.|The weakest currency on our board got weaker news; the yen got clearer news.|The franc did nothing today. The loonie's problems did the work.|Two safe havens, still no winner. One possible twist faded today.|Gold caught its breath, but its biggest enemy is still in the room.")
